    "content": "NASA Headquarters is located in Washington, D.C., but the agency operates ten major field centers and various installations across the United States. Key locations include the Kennedy Space Center (Florida), Johnson Space Center (Houston, Texas), Marshall Space Flight Center (Alabama), and the Jet Propulsion Laboratory (California).Key NASA Locations:NASA Headquarters: 300 E Street SW, Washington, D.C..Kennedy Space Center (KSC): Merritt Island, Florida (Primary launch site).Lyndon B. Johnson Space Center: Houston, Texas (Human spaceflight mission control).Jet Propulsion Laboratory (JPL): La Cañada Flintridge/Pasadena, California (Robotic space exploration).Marshall Space Flight Center: Huntsville, Alabama (Propulsion and engineering).Goddard Space Flight Center: Greenbelt, Maryland (Earth/space science research).Armstrong Flight Research Center: Edwards Air Force Base, California (Atmospheric flight).Glenn Research Center: Cleveland, Ohio (Aerospace technology).Langley Research Center: Hampton, Virginia (Aeronautics).Stennis Space Center: Bay St. Louis, Mississippi (Rocket testing).Ames Research Center: Silicon Valley, California.In addition to these, NASA operates facilities like the Michoud Assembly Facility in New Orleans, LA, and the Wallops Flight Facility in Virginia.",
